      "created_at": "2014-06-20T17:06:47.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Last night on the History Channel they had a show called \"Ancient Ink.\" The first segement was dedicated to Ta Moko of the Maori. Here are some interesting facts about it:</p><ul>\n<li>It is disrepectful for any non-Maori to get a facial tattoo.</li>\n<li>There are specific patterns for specific families.</li>\n<li>The way it was done was to actaully carve scars into the face, let them heal, carve the scars over again, then fill them with pigments.</li>\n<li>The Maori used to mummify the heads.</li>\n<li>They stopped getting facial tattoos when explorers would come and decapitate the people so that they could bring the head home and show it off.</li>\n<li>Recently, they have begun the practice again.</li>\n</ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZYIOjNISsmY\">Here</a> is a link to the show on youtube.</p>",
